# Hellfire Scholar — React Rebuild with Clerk + MongoDB

Rebuild the app as a **React (Vite) frontend** with **Clerk for authentication** and a fresh **Express + MongoDB backend**. The new project lives in the same repo under a `frontend/` + [backend/](file:///Users/shreyanshsachan/Documents/hellfireScholar/backend) split.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph LR
  subgraph Frontend - React + Vite
    A[Landing Page /] --> B[Auth Pages /sign-in, /sign-up]
    B --> C[App Shell /app/*]
    C --> D[Dashboard]
    C --> E[Notes]
    C --> F[Syllabus]
    C --> G[Assignments]
    C --> H[Attendance]
  end
  subgraph Backend - Express
    I[/api/notes]
    J[/api/assignments]
    K[/api/attendance]
    L[/api/syllabus]
    M[/api/user]
  end
  C -- "fetch + Clerk token" --> I & J & K & L & M
  I & J & K & L & M --> N[(MongoDB)]
```

---

## 1. How .env Files Work

### Frontend (`frontend/.env`)
Vite **only** exposes env vars prefixed with `VITE_`. Access them via `import.meta.env.VITE_*`.

```env
# Clerk publishable key (safe for frontend — it's a public key)
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_XXXXXXXXXXXX

# Backend API URL
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
```

**Usage in code:**
```jsx
const API_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL;
```

### Backend (`backend/.env`)
Use `dotenv` to load them. **Never commit this file** — add it to [.gitignore](file:///Users/shreyanshsachan/Documents/hellfireScholar/.gitignore).

```env
# MongoDB connection string (get from MongoDB Atlas)
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster.mongodb.net/hellfireScholar

# Clerk secret key (from Clerk Dashboard → API Keys)
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_XXXXXXXXXXXX

# Server port
PORT=4000
```

**Usage in code:**
```js
require('dotenv').config();
const MONGO_URI = process.env.MONGO_URI;
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Create a Clerk Account first**: Go to [clerk.com](https://clerk.com), create an app, and grab your **Publishable Key** (for frontend) and **Secret Key** (for backend) from **Dashboard → API Keys**.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **MongoDB Atlas**: Create a free cluster at [mongodb.com/atlas](https://mongodb.com/atlas), create a database user, whitelist your IP, and copy the connection string into `MONGO_URI`.

---

## 2. How Routing Works (React Router v6)

The app has **3 layers** of pages:

| Route | Page | Who can see it? |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Landing page | Everyone |
| `/sign-in` | Clerk Sign-In | Signed-out users |
| `/sign-up` | Clerk Sign-Up | Signed-out users |
| `/app` | Dashboard | Signed-in only |
| `/app/notes` | Notes | Signed-in only |
| `/app/syllabus` | Syllabus | Signed-in only |
| `/app/assignments` | Assignments | Signed-in only |
| `/app/attendance` | Attendance | Signed-in only |

### How protection works:
```jsx
// App.jsx — simplified routing structure
<ClerkProvider publishableKey={import.meta.env.VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}>
  <BrowserRouter>
    <Routes>
      {/* Public routes */}
      <Route path="/" element={<LandingPage />} />
      <Route path="/sign-in" element={<SignInPage />} />
      <Route path="/sign-up" element={<SignUpPage />} />

      {/* Protected routes — wrapped in a layout with sidebar */}
      <Route element={<ProtectedLayout />}>
        <Route path="/app" element={<Dashboard />} />
        <Route path="/app/notes" element={<Notes />} />
        <Route path="/app/syllabus" element={<Syllabus />} />
        <Route path="/app/assignments" element={<Assignments />} />
        <Route path="/app/attendance" element={<Attendance />} />
      </Route>
    </Routes>
  </BrowserRouter>
</ClerkProvider>
```

### `ProtectedLayout` — redirects unauthenticated users:
```jsx
import { useAuth } from '@clerk/clerk-react';
import { Navigate, Outlet } from 'react-router-dom';

function ProtectedLayout() {
  const { isSignedIn, isLoaded } = useAuth();
  if (!isLoaded) return <LoadingSpinner />;
  if (!isSignedIn) return <Navigate to="/sign-in" />;
  return (
    <div className="app-shell">
      <Sidebar />
      <main><Outlet /></main>
    </div>
  );
}
```

---

## 3. How Clerk Auth works

### Frontend: `@clerk/clerk-react`
- **`<ClerkProvider>`** wraps your entire app (in `main.jsx`)
- **`<SignIn />`** and **`<SignUp />`** are prebuilt Clerk components — full auth UI out of the box
- **`useUser()`** hook gives you the current user's name, email, avatar
- **`useAuth()`** hook gives you `isSignedIn`, `getToken()` to attach JWT to API calls

### Backend: `@clerk/express`
- **`clerkMiddleware()`** — add as global middleware; it reads the Clerk session token from the request
- **`getAuth(req)`** — extract `userId` from the authenticated request
- **`requireAuth()`** — middleware that returns 401 if not signed in

```js
// backend/server.js
const { clerkMiddleware } = require('@clerk/express');
app.use(clerkMiddleware());

// backend/routes/notes.js — protecting a route
const { requireAuth, getAuth } = require('@clerk/express');

router.get('/', requireAuth(), async (req, res) => {
  const { userId } = getAuth(req);  // Clerk user ID
  const notes = await Note.find({ userId });
  res.json({ notes });
});
```

### How the frontend sends tokens to the backend:
```jsx
import { useAuth } from '@clerk/clerk-react';

function useApi() {
  const { getToken } = useAuth();

  async function apiFetch(path, options = {}) {
    const token = await getToken();
    const res = await fetch(`${import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL}${path}`, {
      ...options,
      headers: {
        ...options.headers,
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`,
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      },
    });
    return res.json();
  }
  return { apiFetch };
}
```

