## 5. Backend API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **User** | | |
| GET | `/api/user/profile` | Get/create user profile (course, subjects) |
| PATCH | `/api/user/profile` | Update course & selected subjects |
| **Notes** | | |
| GET | `/api/notes` | List user's notes (filterable) |
| POST | `/api/notes/upload` | Upload a note file |
| DELETE | `/api/notes/:id` | Delete a note |
| **Assignments** | | |
| GET | `/api/assignments` | List assignments |
| POST | `/api/assignments` | Create assignment |
| PATCH | `/api/assignments/:id` | Update status/marks |
| DELETE | `/api/assignments/:id` | Delete assignment |
| **Attendance** | | |
| GET | `/api/attendance` | List all subject attendance |
| POST | `/api/attendance/mark` | Mark present/absent |
| **Syllabus** | | |
| GET | `/api/syllabus/:subject` | Get completed topics |
| PATCH | `/api/syllabus/:subject/toggle` | Toggle topic completion |

All routes are protected with Clerk's `requireAuth()` middleware.

---

## 6. Phased Build Order

1. **Phase 1** — Scaffold frontend (Vite + React Router + Clerk) + landing page + auth pages
2. **Phase 2** — Build backend (Express + MongoDB + Clerk middleware + all models + routes)
3. **Phase 3** — Build app pages: Dashboard, Notes, Syllabus, Assignments, Attendance
4. **Phase 4** — Polish: dark theme, animations, responsive design

---

## 7. Verification

- **Auth flow**: Landing → Sign Up → redirected to `/app` → Sign Out → back to landing
- **CRUD flows**: Notes, Assignments work end-to-end through the browser
- **Attendance**: Mark present/absent, see dashboard stats update
- **Syllabus**: Toggle topics, see progress bar update
- **Build**: `npm run build` succeeds with zero errors
